python-orjson (3.11.1-1deepin1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Downgrade to upstream 3.11.1 for the Python 3.14 bootstrap with Rust 1.82.
  * Base packaging on Debian 3.11.3-1 and refresh the unwinding patch for 0.2.5.
  * Constrain PyO3 FFI and build-config to the compatible 0.25 series.
  * Declare the minimum Rust version and direct Rust build dependencies.
  * Temporarily omit NumPy, Pandas (which pulls NumPy back in), and Pendulum
    from build-time and autopkgtest dependencies for the Python 3.14 bootstrap.
    Upstream skips their optional tests when these modules are absent; restore
    the dependencies after their rebuilds to recover full test coverage.
  * Also omit the optional Faker tests: python3-fake-factory pulls in the old
    python3-pil binary, which is not installable with Python 3.14.

 -- purofle <purofle@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:59:01 +0800

